# /etc/default/astro-process on puppy.
#
# REFERENCE COPY ONLY — see roles/astro-processor in the ansible repo for
# the live rendering (`astro_processor_cameras`).
#
# HISTORY: puppy once processed every camera, because the Pis wrote to
# puppy's NFS export and a Pi reading its own frames back over NFS was
# ~13x slower (astrocam backfill, 2026-06-20). That is no longer the
# layout. As of 2026-08:
#
#   eclipticam-v1 / eclipticam-v3w -> processed ON eclipticam (local SSD)
#   astrocam                       -> processed ON muppet (frames on bigstore)
#
# so puppy names NO cameras. The dispatcher requires exactly one host's
# CAMERAS list to name each camera (see bin/astro-process); listing a
# camera here as well as on its real host is a slow duplicate, not a
# fallback. astro-process.service is disabled on puppy.
CAMERAS=""
